#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Ticket Integration
	Testing ticket sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate static variables for a support user
	* I rename the first support user variables
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue1}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue1}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastNameValue1}  |
	* I generate static variables for a support user
	* I rename the second support user variables
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue2}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue2}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue2} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastNameValue2}  |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code     | OSBZENOSBZEN                  | |
	| Language | English                       | |
	| Name     | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region   | United States                 | |
	| Status   | Active                        | |
	| Tier     | T1                            | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I generate static variables for a support user
	* I rename the third support user variables
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue3}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue3}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue3} |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                       |
	| Group         | Employees                       |
	* I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" added via automatic sync
	* the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" via automatic sync
	* I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	* I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	* I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	* I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	* I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	* I update the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" to have the role "Agent"

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	| ${staticEmailValue3} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	| ${staticEmailValue3} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	| ${staticEmailValue3} |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	| ${staticEmailValue3} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	| ${staticEmailValue3} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	| ${staticEmailValue3} |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "noreply@liferay.com" the recipient is "zendesk-admin@liferay.com" with the email address "zendesk-admin@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "Reassign Tickets and Downgrade Full Agent"

Scenario: View ticket after employee deactivation
	Zendesk tickets should remain assigned to an employee even after the employee has been deactivated

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	Then the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}"
	And I deactivate the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" from okta
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should not be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should not be in the organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should not have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "${staticContactFirstNameValue3} ${staticContactLastNameValue3}"	
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the role "Agent"
	And the ticket with the ticket ID "${staticRequestIdList}" should be assigned to the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}"
	When I go the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "noreply@liferay.com" the recipient is "zendesk-admin@liferay.com" with the email address "zendesk-admin@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "Reassign Tickets and Downgrade Full Agent"
	Then I should be able to view the email message containing the following text
	| Please downgrade ${staticContactFirstNameValue3} ${staticContactLastNameValue3} ${staticEmailValue3} on Zendesk. They have the following non-closed tickets assigned to them. |
	And I should be able to view the email message containing the following text
	| ${staticRequestIdList} |

Scenario: View solved ticket after employee deactivation
	Employees should not be deactivated with zendesk solved tickets assigned to them

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	Then the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}"
	And I generate past static start and end dates
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Portal Production" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Gold Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "solved"
	When I deactivate the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" from okta
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should not be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should not be in the organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should not have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "${staticContactFirstNameValue3} ${staticContactLastNameValue3}"
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the role "Agent"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the default user from the organization with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" as the requester
	When I go the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "noreply@liferay.com" the recipient is "zendesk-admin@liferay.com" with the email address "zendesk-admin@liferay.com" and the message content contains the text "Reassign Tickets and Downgrade Full Agent"
	Then I should be able to view the email message containing the following text
	| Please downgrade ${staticContactFirstNameValue3} ${staticContactLastNameValue3} ${staticEmailValue3} on Zendesk. They have the following non-closed tickets assigned to them. |
	And I should be able to view the email message containing the following text
	| ${staticRequestIdList} |

Scenario: View closed ticket after employee deactivation
	Employees should be deactivated even with zendesk closed tickets assigned to them

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Portal Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | licenses                 | 1 |
	| Product Field and Value | version                  | 6 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Gold Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	Then the support organization with the code "OSBZENOSBZEN" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" should be in the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}                    |
	And I assign the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to a user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}"
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	And I change the status of the ticket with the ID "${staticRequestIdList}" to "closed"
	And I deactivate the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" from okta
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should not be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	# Necessary pause for tags and zendesk org sync. Analyze if can be taken out or reduced once account index improves
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should not be in the organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" should not have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "${staticContactFirstNameValue3} ${staticContactLastNameValue3}"
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue3}" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the role "End User"